omni-server
===========

This service wraps third-party components that are NOT covered by this repo's
MIT LICENSE and are NOT redistributed here — they are fetched at setup time by
`scripts/setup_vendor.py` (source) and `scripts/download_weights.py` (weights).
You are responsible for complying with their terms.

1. Microsoft OmniParser (source code)
   - https://github.com/microsoft/OmniParser  (pinned at commit b0d5c9f)
   - Vendored into `vendor/OmniParser`; we import `util/utils.py` (patched, see
     `patches/`) and `util/box_annotator.py`.
   - Upstream code license: MIT (see the upstream repo's LICENSE for the
     authoritative, current terms).

2. OmniParser v2 model weights
   - https://huggingface.co/microsoft/OmniParser-v2.0
   - `icon_detect/` — a YOLO-based icon detector. YOLO/Ultralytics-derived
     weights are commonly distributed under AGPL-3.0; review the model card
     before any commercial/closed deployment.
   - `icon_caption_florence/` — a Florence-2-based caption model (MIT-family).
   - Confirm the exact license on the model card; terms can change.

3. Florence-2 processor / base
   - https://huggingface.co/microsoft/Florence-2-base
   - Fetched by `transformers` at first model load (tokenizer + remote modeling
     code, `trust_remote_code=True`).

4. OCR engines: PaddleOCR (Apache-2.0), EasyOCR (Apache-2.0).

Because the icon-detector weights may be AGPL-licensed, treat the *running
service* accordingly if you expose it as a network service to third parties.
For an internal, single-operator deployment this is typically fine; verify for
your situation.
